    ports/vigo: promote port-map heading to h2, document reshuffle review
    
    Closes the Vigo branch of the careful-not-clever cleanup. Reading the
    page top-to-bottom found two things:
    
    1. The section reshuffle from commit 495a860a was directionally
       correct (the original Vigo had cruise-port, getting-around, and
       excursions dumped after FAQ at the bottom of the page; the new
       order — hero, logbook, cruise-port, getting-around, port-map,
       excursions, weather-guide, depth-soundings, faq — reads naturally:
       terminal location → transport → visual orientation → things to do
       → reference material). The transition sentences between each
       moved pair work; this part of the reshuffle is left as-is.
    
    2. The port-map section's summary still used <h3>Vigo Area Map</h3>.
       That heading level was correct when the map was nested inside
       weather-guide (its original location, where it was a sub-element
       of the weather section). After being pulled out and promoted to a
       top-level <details class="port-section">, the heading should be
       <h2> to match the other 380+ ports (Adelaide Area Map, Acapulco
       Area Map, Agadir Area Map, etc. all use <h2>). Left as <h3>, the
       page had a heading hierarchy gap (h2 Getting Around → h3 Vigo
       Area Map → h2 Excursions) that affects screen-reader navigation.
    
    Fix: <h3> → <h2> on line 391. No other changes.
    
    What this does NOT cover: a real browser walk of the page. The flow
    review here was textual (read each section's opening sentence to
    verify transitions). A future reviewer should still open the page in
    a browser and confirm the visual layout works at the breakpoints
    the CSS targets — column widths, the map's interactive controls,
    and the way the activity-row block lays out alongside the rest of
    the weather guide. Per
    admin/CAREFUL_NOT_CLEVER_FAILURE_2026_05_21.md §4 (section reshuffle
    without reader check), this commit is the textual-flow check; a
    browser walk is still owed.
    
    Validators: vigo.html PASSES both port validators (58/100 on the
    v2 page validator, 55-pass on the weather sub-validator). Warnings
    in the v2 report are content-quality items pre-dating this commit.
    
    Pattern reference: admin/CAREFUL_NOT_CLEVER_FAILURE_2026_05_21.md §4
    (section reshuffle without reader check).
    
